When shrinking:
- The buffer stays at the same address (realloc in-place)
- The "freed" portion after the shrunk buffer might be reused
- The stale pointer still points to the original memory

When growing:
- The buffer might move if there's not enough space
- The old buffer is freed
- The stale pointer points to freed memory

